WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.870
Eleven acceptance tests and forty-two
integration tests passed in the shared stack,

2
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.720
against a pull request's own
image, before anyone merged it.

3
00:00:17.232 --> 00:00:20.002
Service path. Ship it through the line.

4
00:00:20.822 --> 00:00:23.912
What happens to my change
after I open a pull request?

5
00:00:25.368 --> 00:00:27.288
You proved your change from your desk.

6
00:00:27.288 --> 00:00:31.360
Open a pull request, and the
fork's rules for main take over.

7
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.410
Two checks must pass:

8
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.370
CodeQL, and Validation Summary.

9
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.960
Validation Summary speaks
for the build, the image,

10
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.490
and the lane: your image's
run in a real stack.

11
00:00:43.984 --> 00:00:45.464
And a person must approve:

12
00:00:45.464 --> 00:00:48.034
a code owner, after your last push.

13
00:00:48.184 --> 00:00:53.394
A new push dismisses the approval, and
every review thread must be resolved.

14
00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.238
Here's one change through the line:

15
00:00:57.388 --> 00:01:01.958
a one-line fix in the fork's Azure
code, from a branch in the fork itself.

16
00:01:02.348 --> 00:01:04.908
A pull request from
another repository builds,

17
00:01:04.908 --> 00:01:06.918
but gets no image and no lane.

18
00:01:08.384 --> 00:01:11.584
Validation built it in three
minutes, and pushed an image,

19
00:01:11.584 --> 00:01:13.274
named by its digest.

20
00:01:13.424 --> 00:01:16.874
Then Deploy Gate let the
run borrow the shared stack.

21
00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.150
The first try failed.

22
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.380
The shared environment wasn't ready:

23
00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:26.270
Deploy and Test waited ten minutes,
and stopped before it pinned anything.

24
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.510
Validation Summary went red.

25
00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:32.046
It wasn't the change.

26
00:01:32.276 --> 00:01:37.156
Once the environment reported Deployable,
Re-run failed jobs ran the lane again,

27
00:01:37.156 --> 00:01:38.366
on the same image.

28
00:01:38.516 --> 00:01:41.676
It pinned that digest, passed
eleven and forty-two tests,

29
00:01:41.676 --> 00:01:43.566
and put the canonical image back.

30
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.610
The same comment turned green in place.

31
00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.010
Read its Deploy and Test row:

32
00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.610
when the lane is skipped,
the note says why.

33
00:01:54.744 --> 00:01:57.154
After the merge, main builds again.

34
00:01:57.384 --> 00:02:00.344
The merge commit is a new
build with a new digest,

35
00:02:00.344 --> 00:02:03.794
so the push run proves that
one too, in the same lane.

36
00:02:06.172 --> 00:02:07.502
An easy mistake:

37
00:02:07.572 --> 00:02:11.102
the stack only ever runs
released versions of a fork.

38
00:02:11.652 --> 00:02:16.062
This fix ran in the shared stack
twice, and no release holds it yet.

39
00:02:16.372 --> 00:02:19.102
The latest release came
out hours before it,

40
00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:22.062
and the release pull
request is still open.

41
00:02:22.612 --> 00:02:27.182
A release, when it comes, tags
an image that already exists.

42
00:02:27.332 --> 00:02:31.502
Check with gh release list,
beside the lane's run on main.

43
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.530
So now you can say:

44
00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.600
two checks and a code owner's
approval gate my pull request,

45
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.690
and the lane runs my image in a
real stack before any release.

46
00:02:46.008 --> 00:02:49.858
Next: what does the line ask
of me when upstream moves?

